# Cursor AI Rules for Social Commerce Platform

## Project Context
This is an AI-powered social commerce platform for India, built with:
- Backend: FastAPI microservices with MySQL
- Frontend: React Native (mobile) + Next.js (web)
- AI/ML: PyTorch, OpenAI GPT-4, custom recommendation models

## Code Style

### Python
- Use type hints for all function parameters and return types
- Follow PEP 8 style guide
- Use f-strings for string formatting
- Prefer async/await for I/O operations
- Document functions with docstrings (Google style)

### Database
- Use MySQL 8.0 as primary database
- Use SQLAlchemy ORM, not raw SQL
- All models should inherit from BaseModel in shared/database/models.py
- Use proper indexes on foreign keys and frequently queried columns
- Use JSON columns for flexible data (media_urls, product_tags, etc.)

### API Design
- Use RESTful conventions
- Return proper HTTP status codes
- Use Pydantic models for request/response validation
- Include pagination for list endpoints (skip, limit)
- Use consistent error response format

### Authentication
- Use JWT tokens for authentication
- Token should include user_id in "sub" claim
- Use shared/auth utilities for consistency
- Protect endpoints with get_current_user dependency

## File Structure
- Each microservice in backend/services/<service-name>/src/
- Shared utilities in backend/shared/
- Use __init__.py files for proper package structure
- Keep service-specific code isolated

## Naming Conventions
- Database tables: plural, lowercase (users, posts, products)
- Model classes: singular, PascalCase (User, Post, Product)
- API endpoints: kebab-case (/users/me, /products/{id})
- Variables: snake_case
- Constants: UPPER_SNAKE_CASE

## Error Handling
- Use HTTPException from FastAPI with appropriate status codes
- Provide clear error messages
- Log errors appropriately
- Don't expose internal errors to clients

## Testing
- Write tests for all services
- Use pytest for Python tests
- Mock external dependencies
- Test both success and error cases

## Performance
- Use database indexes appropriately
- Implement caching with Redis where beneficial
- Use connection pooling for database
- Optimize queries (avoid N+1 problems)

## Security
- Never commit secrets or API keys
- Use environment variables for configuration
- Hash passwords with bcrypt
- Validate and sanitize all inputs
- Use CORS middleware appropriately

## AI/ML Integration
- Keep ML models in backend/ml/
- Use separate endpoints for ML inference
- Cache model predictions when appropriate
- Monitor model performance

## When Adding New Features
1. Create database models first
2. Create Pydantic schemas
3. Implement API endpoints
4. Add error handling
5. Write tests
6. Update documentation
